WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.560
Welcome to Ear Biscuits,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.420
the podcast where two lifelong friends

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.640
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.473
I'm Rhett.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:10.350
And I'm Link.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.800
This week at the round
table of Dim Lighting.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.500
We're wrapping up the year

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.000
with one of my favorite episodes

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.490
that we do at the end of every year.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:25.490
Our Top 10 moments this year, 2022.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.407
Now, I know that you're having,

00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:30.450
you're having a rough time today

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.500
and it kind of, I mean,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.180
you look the part, I gotta--

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.013
Really?

00:00:34.013 --> 00:00:34.980
I gotta admit.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.260
Like no, I'm just saying that like,

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.610
when I came in this morning,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.923
you were already lying on the couch.

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:43.560
When we're recording this,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.530
you're still pretty
early on in your injury.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.004
You're still, you're adjusting to it.

00:00:49.004 --> 00:00:51.193
I do want you to know that

00:00:51.193 --> 00:00:55.018
your wife called me this morning,

00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:57.180
after you left.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.013
Oh yeah.

00:00:58.013 --> 00:00:58.846
Just--

00:00:58.846 --> 00:00:59.937
Okay, I know what she said.

00:00:59.937 --> 00:01:01.530
No, just to let me know that

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.850
you're having a difficult time.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:03.930
I did not tell her

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.130
that I was taking a
crap when she called me.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.520
I guess I'm telling her that now.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.090
But she may have noticed
the echo in my voice.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.530
You didn't like flush in the middle--

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.363
No, I didn't.

00:01:14.363 --> 00:01:15.930
In fact, I stopped.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.910
No actual defecation took place

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.810
while I was talking to your wife,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.580
because I felt like that
would be inappropriate.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.840
I'm just letting you know.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.376
But I was, I answered it,

00:01:23.376 --> 00:01:24.209
'cause I was like,

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.042
Christie doesn't usually call me.

00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:25.875
Is everything okay?

00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:27.637
Like, I thought she was gonna say

00:01:27.637 --> 00:01:29.280
something like, Link
broke his other shoulder

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.480
or something like, you know,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.620
but she just said that you're having

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.750
a difficult time just getting ready,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.583
getting out of the house.

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:35.416
And then when I came in,

00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:37.877
you're lying down and you look,

00:01:37.877 --> 00:01:41.100
you look frazzled.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.516
Like you haven't been
able to shave, obviously.

00:01:43.516 --> 00:01:45.360
You're growing your Kenny Rogers beard

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.410
and your hair still looks like

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.361
you started with your left hand.

00:01:48.361 --> 00:01:50.040
You're in the early stages.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.120
You're gonna figure this out.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:51.960
I'm here for you.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:52.950
I'm just acknowledging that

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.270
you're going through a difficult time.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.133
That's sweet that Christie called you,

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.773
which brings me to my number 10.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.530
You know, we each made our list.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.000
We didn't share these with each other,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.043
so we're gonna go in reverse order.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.410
Yeah, I decided to put

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.820
breaking my collarbone as my

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.380
number 10 moment of the year,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.524
because it's very fresh on my mind.

00:02:12.524 --> 00:02:14.007
Only number 10?

00:02:14.007 --> 00:02:17.910
Well, one of my criteria

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.090
for making my list was, you know,

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.060
at our age it's hard
to make core memories,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.980
something that then sticks with you

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.020
for the rest of your life.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.750
But I think easily

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.520
making that one of the criteria,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.810
breaking my collarbone

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.390
becomes one of my core memories.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.820
So it's, I think it had to go on my list.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.866
Oh, easily.

00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:41.298
You know, for it to be,

00:02:41.298 --> 00:02:44.550
it could be six weeks of recovery here,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.503
maybe more, hopefully less.

00:02:47.394 --> 00:02:51.208
Still haven't had my ortho follow up,

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:52.433
so I don't know exactly what's going on,

00:02:52.433 --> 00:02:55.500
or started any PT, anything like that.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.769
But yeah, I will always remember

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:01.800
that I broke my clavicle.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.633
Mm.

00:03:02.633 --> 00:03:04.760
Because I always remember
breaking my pelvis

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.510
and that's the only
thing that I've broken.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.950
Just your pelvis and your clavicle.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.750
Yeah, so,

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.400
I mean this is kind of a big moment

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.270
towards the end of the year

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.636
here for me.

00:03:16.636 --> 00:03:17.565
And, yeah--

00:03:17.565 --> 00:03:18.398
And it remains to be seen

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.231
how much of an impact it will

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.190
continue to have.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:22.319
I was, I mean,

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:24.360
I know for Good Mythical Morning,

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.550
like yeah.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.810
'Cause I mean, through January,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.672
I'm gonna be in freaking sling

00:03:29.672 --> 00:03:31.740
for the episodes.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:32.700
Yeah.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.370
So, yeah, this morning was tough.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.900
I'm still making an adjustment.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.733
I'm...

00:03:38.627 --> 00:03:41.787
The worst part of my day is getting up

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:42.930
and getting going.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.630
I mean it's, everything has to change.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.586
And I've been like,

00:03:46.586 --> 00:03:47.730
you know what I'm gonna have,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.920
I'm gonna have a positive
attitude about this.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.190
I'm gonna see this as an opportunity

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.660
or a series of opportunities.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.170
But man, it just kind of beats you down

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.390
when it's, you just can't
get anything together.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.160
Like, so I finally got ready,

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.783
I got everything done and like,

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.540
I was about to leave.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.480
I was putting on my socks and shoes.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.313
And I don't want to,

00:04:10.313 --> 00:04:12.750
I don't wanna ask Christie and the kids

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.710
to help me do everything,

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.900
'cause I want to figure out,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.570
if this is a many-weeks process,

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.410
I don't want it to be like,

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.450
every time I put on socks,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.277
for a member of my family to come over

00:04:23.277 --> 00:04:25.277
and like hold half of the sock.

00:04:25.277 --> 00:04:26.730
Right, right.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.563
So I finally,

00:04:27.563 --> 00:04:28.470
I get on my socks and my shoes

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.553
and I'm just like,

00:04:30.913 --> 00:04:31.746
Chrissy's in the kitchen

00:04:31.746 --> 00:04:33.905
and I go over to her and I'm like,

00:04:33.905 --> 00:04:35.877
"I need a hug."

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.208
Because I'm like, okay, if you,

00:04:39.208 --> 00:04:40.770
I'm learning to,

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.720
and this will be another point

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.870
on my list today.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.570
But just learning to express my needs

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.760
in a way that is appropriate, right?

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.410
So it's like, for me it's like,

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.243
I need a hug.

00:04:53.243 --> 00:04:54.390
So then Christie like,

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.640
stops what she's doing and she,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.990
I tried to, I had to tell her how

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.280
to give me a hug.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.540
But no, don't, not too tight.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.770
Don't put the arm up here.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.603
Put the arm--

00:05:02.603 --> 00:05:03.860
I need a side hug.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:04.693
Down here.

00:05:04.693 --> 00:05:06.513
I needed a, I definitely
needed a front hug.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.350
And then, I'm just hugging her

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.110
for a prolonged period.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:13.943
Okay.

00:05:13.943 --> 00:05:17.857
And then with my head on her shoulder.

00:05:17.857 --> 00:05:19.773
And then she's like,

00:05:21.217 --> 00:05:26.217
"Are you crying or are you laughing?"

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.463
And I'm like, both.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.468
I would do both, man.

00:05:32.468 --> 00:05:34.233
It's okay, man.

00:05:35.631 --> 00:05:36.464
It's okay.

00:05:36.464 --> 00:05:37.470
Let it out, man.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.630
It's just like this frustration

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.270
and I'm still really grateful

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.640
that I'm not really in any pain.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.160
So it's really just this frustration

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.190
of like trying to get together.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.367
Yep.

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:52.500
And then the amount of,

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.880
I don't know, it's just like,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:54.930
so I was laying on the couch

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.190
when I got here, 'cause I was like,

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:00.660
I told you, I'm just, it's exhausting.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.633
It's exhausting to figure this stuff out.

00:06:02.633 --> 00:06:04.770
You know how I think about things like,

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.540
oh, my systems are broken.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.466
Yeah, it's especially hard on you--

00:06:08.466 --> 00:06:09.851
It's hard on me, but it's--

00:06:09.851 --> 00:06:10.684
Because you do things exactly

00:06:10.684 --> 00:06:12.210
a certain way that you've perfected

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.043
in each step.

00:06:13.043 --> 00:06:14.790
So when every single step

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:15.723
has been compromised, that's--

00:06:15.723 --> 00:06:17.100
It's been cut in half.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.650
It's like the dominant
arm has been taken away.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.740
So I'm really, excuse me,

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.930
I'm really trying to see
it as an opportunity.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.630
It's like, what can I learn from this?

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.010
How can I, you know,

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.930
it could be a lot worse.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.763
Chrissy was like,

00:06:31.763 --> 00:06:33.390
"Thank God you didn't hit your head.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.500
You know, that could have,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.760
that could have altered your life

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.650
for many years, if not forever."

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.899
And I was like, how do you know that?

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.262
She was like, "I've done some reading."

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.070
Opportunity for your left arm.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.990
Once I get here, I'm...

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.730
The worst part's over.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.190
Like, that's how I look at it.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.023
Well, if you need a hug,

00:06:57.023 --> 00:06:57.900
just let me know.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.280
So I'll be laughing

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.660
and crying on your shoulder.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.641
I mean it, I was legitimately thinking

00:07:02.641 --> 00:07:05.370
about afterward as I was driving in,

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.080
I was like, you know the phrase

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.220
a shoulder to cry on?

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.540
It's like, yes,

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.950
I actually took advantage

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.570
of a shoulder to cry on.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.060
And that's a good thing.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.180
That's a good thing.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.280
It did help.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.595
You know, you got--

00:07:18.595 --> 00:07:19.428
I'm sure your wife, you know, enjoyed it.

00:07:19.428 --> 00:07:20.460
I think she like, did she?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.450
So when she called you,

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.983
did she go into that detail?

00:07:22.983 --> 00:07:25.080
She's like, he was like
crying and laughing

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.205
at the same time.

00:07:26.205 --> 00:07:27.038
I think she said that

00:07:27.038 --> 00:07:27.871
he broke down a little bit.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.200
So I did not picture you

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.370
just crying on her shoulder.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:33.273
But now I do.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.300
Well it was a beautiful moment.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.830
One of my top 10 moments--

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:40.770
It's all downhill from here,

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.132
is that, it's probably
too soon to use that joke

00:07:43.132 --> 00:07:45.540
because that's how you hurt yourself.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.373
Yeah.

00:07:46.373 --> 00:07:47.400
Going down hill.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.040
So I put that in my number 10, man.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:55.040
My number 10 is adopting
Sean, our new dog.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:56.880
I love the look on your face.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.680
He made the list.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.300
Sean is really growing on me.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.713
I love that little guy.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.790
He, as a matter of fact,

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.400
Jesse, you know, was recently,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.110
she was, when we went to North Carolina,

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.180
she stayed a little bit longer

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.110
working on some stuff.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.430
And so Shep and I came back

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.500
and so I had some time with him

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.540
and that's good.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.520
He's really connecting with me.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.930
And you saw the other day

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.610
when we were having all those meetings

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.607
at the creative house,

00:08:25.607 --> 00:08:28.144
just, you know, digital meetings.

00:08:28.144 --> 00:08:31.226
He's coming up to me all the time.

00:08:31.226 --> 00:08:33.000
He came up to you and jumped

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:33.833
right in your lap.

00:08:33.833 --> 00:08:34.950
Right when we came, when I came over.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.150
I was shocked,

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.250
'cause I had a hat on and--

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.083
He's afraid of hats.

00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:40.620
I thought he was jumping in my lap

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.200
to like, to eat my crotch.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.160
I shouldn't have said it that way.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:44.993
Yeah.

00:08:44.993 --> 00:08:45.826
To bite me.

00:08:45.826 --> 00:08:47.940
Like he did the last time,

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.634
I came to work and he was there.

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:50.467
Yeah, he bit you twice.

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:51.677
But you said

00:08:51.677 --> 00:08:52.510
it was because he was on a leash,

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.730
but he was like, yeah,

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.563
he jumped up on my lap.

00:08:54.563 --> 00:08:55.650
I think he's an accepted petting.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.480
He's a learning to trust people.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.440
He's a learning.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.760
He's learning to trust people,

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.242
whatever, wherever he came from,

00:09:02.242 --> 00:09:03.075
that he developed reasons

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:03.908
to not trust people

00:09:03.908 --> 00:09:05.550
and to not trust strangers.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.810
Mm-hmm.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:07.980
And so I, you know,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.882
he's still in the house,

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:12.038
but it's a little bit more,

00:09:12.038 --> 00:09:14.730
a little bit easier to deal with.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.780
He's so cute.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:16.770
His hair's growing in,

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:17.910
he's actually becoming like--

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:18.750
He's more attractive.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.030
He's becoming the dog that I clicked on.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.410
Right.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.760
On the website to adopt him.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.666
He's a lot more pettable.

00:09:25.666 --> 00:09:27.870
And so he, and you know what?

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.510
He remains a challenge and an opportunity.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.010
Not quite like your clavicle.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:33.300
There you go.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.600
